What changed
------------

The fork is the render worker for Inkmirage Colophon. It is not the public
latex.ytotech.com service.

- Each job runs in a new rootless Podman container (`--network=none`,
  read-only root, 512 MiB tmpfs, non-root user, 1 CPU, 2048 MiB memory,
  256 pids, 60 s wall clock, 20 MiB output cap). The container is removed
  afterwards. The result is returned in the HTTP response and is not kept.
- LaTeX shell-escape is off (`-no-shell-escape`, and `shell_escape = f` in
  the image texmf). The host compiler path raises rather than running TeX
  on the worker host.
- The listener binds only to a configured Tailscale address. It refuses to
  start if that address is unset, unspecified (0.0.0.0 or ::), a LAN
  address, loopback, or any other non-Tailscale address.
- Every request needs the shared worker token (Bearer). Concurrency is one
  job per process. A second job is refused at once with Retry-After. There
  is no queue.
- New jobs are refused when the 1-minute load average is above 3.0, when
  MemAvailable is below 4096 MiB, or when the load sample is stale or
  unreadable. An unreadable kill-switch file is treated as engaged.
- Spawn failures, Pandoc failures, diagram failures, and LaTeX failures
  fail closed. A wall-clock kill is `failTimeout`, which is not a render
  error. Output over 20 MiB is `failCapHit`.
- `POST /builds/sync` still accepts a single inline TeX or Markdown resource,
  but URL, git, tar, and cache resources are rejected, and the only compiler
  is XeLaTeX.
- The image bakes a trimmed TeX Live (XeLaTeX, xeCJK, Noto CJK TC, TikZ,
  CircuiTikZ) plus Pandoc, the pandoc-ext/diagram Lua filter, mermaid-cli
  with headless Chromium, d2, and a vendored PIDcircuitTikZ. There is no
  runtime package fetch and no Tectonic. `tlmgr` is removed from the image.

Third-party pieces added with this fork
----------------------------------------

- pandoc-ext/diagram, commit 5aaf35e6f775ddf501045fe28b03642ee73db2f4,
  MIT, with two local edits (see vendor/diagram/README.md). SHA-256 of the
  vendored diagram.lua:
  b8e65d171bcf62475e0ec93cb77bbbcc66dd501f8e91a49fcfecf912e5842fae.
  Debian `librsvg2-bin` supplies `rsvg-convert`, which Pandoc uses to place
  SVG diagrams in a PDF.
- PIDcircuitTikZ by Jelle Spijker, MIT. There is no CTAN package of this
  name (CTAN search, 2026-09-26). It is not CircuiTikZ. CircuiTikZ is the
  CTAN package `circuitikz`. TikZ is delivered by CTAN package `pgf`.
  xeCJK is CTAN package `xecjk`. Debian bookworm ships it in
  `texlive-lang-cjk` as `xeCJK.sty` (kpathsea is case-sensitive). Noto CJK
  TC is installed from Debian `fonts-noto-cjk`, not from CTAN.

`McpResponse.retryAfterSec` is unbound in the Colophon SysML model. This
worker uses 10 seconds. `McpGate.maxInputKiB` is also unbound; the worker
refuses request bodies above 16 MiB as a local transport cap.
